    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0359" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10518</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-29T14:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2201. Your 3744, June 24, 9 a.m., and 3782, June 26, 5 p.m. Department desires
                    that you carefully watch the activities of the Bulgarians, reporting to the
                    Department from time to time, but abstain wholly from conversations with them or
                    with Turks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
